What do you boys do to celebrate back home?

85
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,240
Celebrate?

86
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,340
It's almost New Year's in the real world, isn't it?

87
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,960
Time flows at the same speed in here as it does outside.

88
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:52,620
Oh, no!

89
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:53,080
Hmm?

90
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:54,580
I forgot!

91
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:57,160
The deadline for the hunter exhibit coming up!

92
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:58,680
Oh, man.

93
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,360
And right when training was starting to get kind of fun, too.

94
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:05,320
If my memory serves, you have to apply by year's end.

95
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,620
Then we need to hurry!

96
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,060
But remind me how we get outside again?

97
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:12,200
I'm guessing there are spell cards to leave the game, right?

98
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:13,320
There are.

99
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,720
So let's take another trip to Masadora.

100
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:17,200
All right!

101
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:22,160
Now, let's find a place to have some tea.

102
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,200
We can't.

103
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,680
We don't have much time.

104
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,860
We can ask at the stores we go to.

105
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:29,820
You want to leave the island?

106
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,360
No sweat.

107
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,980
That'll be 3,000 jenny.

108
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:40,360
If you go about 50 kilometers west, you'll reach the island's only port.

109
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,180
You'll have to defeat or bribe the harbormaster.

110
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:46,740
If you do, you'll get a ticket that'll transport you outside.

111
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,420
How big of a bribe do you think?

112
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,680
That depends on how he's feeling.

113
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:52,500
Yeah, okay.

114
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,840
Your other option is to use a leave spell card.

115
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:59,120
But that one is pretty rare, so...

116
00:06:59,120 --> 00:06:59,980
What do we do?

117
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:01,160
Head to the port.

118
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:05,160
Since it's a rare card, it might not even show up no matter how much we spend.

119
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,300
Yeah, you're right.

120
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:16,920
Voila!

121
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:21,720
Well, I guess now I'll go ace the exam and come right back.

122
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:25,060
First, go to the lone cedar tree that's down by Dole Harbor.

123
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:27,420
Magical beasts called Kiriko live there.

124
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:31,360
Just tell them that you're my friend, and they'll take you right to the exam site.

125
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,200
Will do.

126
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,300
See ya!

127
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,980
All right then.

128
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:40,680
Let's get back to your training.

129
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:41,940
Us!

130
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:54,900
Welcome, sir.

131
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:57,400
Is this where I started?

132
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,100
No, it's not.

133
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,440
The girl looks familiar, though.

134
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:05,100
But that's pretty typical for games.

135
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,480
Will you be leaving the island now?

136
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:10,220
If so, please specify your location.

137
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:12,840
Do you have Dole Harbor?

138
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:14,200
Yes, I do.

139
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:16,180
Then just send me there.

140
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:17,800
I understand.

141
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:24,400
When you leave this island, all of the cards that are in your free slots will be deleted instantly.

142
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:25,800
Do you accept that?

143
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:27,200
Yeah, that's fine.

144
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:31,560
Well, in that case, we will be patiently awaiting your return, sir.

145
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:40,040
Guess I'm back in the real world now, huh?

146
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,960
Doesn't feel any different.

147
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,280
And book.

148
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,540
So it doesn't work out here.

149
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:48,540
Gotcha.

150
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:53,600
I'll submit my application and head for that cedar tree.

151
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:57,200
But first, I've got to shower and change.

152
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,320
Okay.

153
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,360
We'll train the whole time you're running.

154
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:06,000
When you can form numbers zero through nine, all within one minute, you pass.

155
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:08,260
Huh?

156
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:10,260
That hurt!

157
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:14,360
What in the world are you doing?

158
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:15,260
Huh?

159
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:21,260
Aren't you...

160
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:24,260
I can see that your other friend isn't with you.

161
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:26,780
What's that thing on your shoulder?

162
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,160
What happened to you?

163
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:29,060
Is something wrong?

164
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,180
The bomber got us.

165
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:32,420
Hear me out.

166
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:34,020
I have something to say.

167
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:45,860
So he was the bomber.

168
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:50,400
The others are back in our hideout, waiting for him to disarm the bombs.

169
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:55,380
They believe in the terms he gave them, but I'm not as convinced.

170
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,140
Now what?

171
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,420
What can we do?

172
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,900
If they're prepared to accept casualties...

173
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:01,500
Won't happen.

174
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:06,580
The very first ones to jump him will be the first ones to be sacrificed.

175
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:09,340
Who would ever volunteer for that?

176
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,760
Good point.

177
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:16,420
Jispa was the most proficient of us in combat, yet he was beaten instantly.

178
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:19,440
We were already doomed at that point.

179
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:24,080
And allowing Genthro to leave the game proved to be a fatal mistake.

180
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:31,400
We foolishly began to celebrate before we had the chance to verify each member's cards and assigned roles.

181
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,600
And that was when he caught us off guard.

182
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:39,080
I hate to say it, but I...

183
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:43,720
I was so distracted that I simply didn't see him use leave until it was too late.

184
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:49,120
You were probably focused on his explanation, trying to figure out its meaning.

185
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,100
Yeah.

186
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:54,560
We were thrust into that situation with absolutely no warning at all.

187
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:58,220
Of course, we were all too stunned to take any action.

188
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,340
I see.

189
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,940
But may I ask why you're telling us all this?

190
00:11:01,940 --> 00:11:08,340
Out of everyone I've met here on the island, I believe you're the ones I can rely on the most.

191
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:14,900
If you communicate with any other players, I beg you to tell them all about the bomber.

192
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:18,920
If they know about his ability, they can guard against it.

193
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:23,280
And if it comes down to it, I want you to try to avenge us.

194
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:27,320
At the very least, do not let him clear the game.

195
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,220
We understand.

196
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:32,560
Thank you.

197
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:39,680
I'll use what little time I have left to tell as many as I can about the bomber.

198
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:41,360
Book.

199
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,360
Return on!

200
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:44,080
Bunzin!

201
00:11:53,280 --> 00:12:00,660
Actually, the truth of the matter is that when I used Magnetic Force, those two were the only players I could find.

202
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:03,920
But flattery works wonders.

203
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:09,300
When it comes to deactivating someone's nin, every thousandth of a percent counts.

204
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:14,660
Now then, Nyx has probably gone off to meet with the bombers.

205
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:20,660
However, if what they promised turns out to be a mass-dead nation...

206
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,160
...better get started.

207
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,560
You're finally here.

208
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,120
Now, hand over your ring.

209
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:39,660
Jispa has passed away.

210
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:41,320
That's nice.

211
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:42,360
Your ring?

212
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,260
Disarm everyone's bums first!

213
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:46,920
Hell no.

214
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:50,540
First, I have to take that ring back inside the game.

215
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:54,440
And once I do, I'll confirm that all the cards are indeed in the binder.

216
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:57,660
Then I'll disarm the bombs.

217
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,820
This is the last time.

218
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:02,740
Hand over the ring.

219
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:12,080
Sub, go ahead and put it on.

220
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:18,380
If you put on a second ring when you're outside the game, your original data gets overwritten.

221
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:19,200
Mm-hmm.

222
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,540
Now then, let's head back inside together.

223
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:24,240
Hold on.

224
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:25,840
What's your name again?

225
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:39,140
Migamora, Samingadora, Interaminga, Zinberalubra.

226
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:44,840
Spirits of the forest, remove the unclean nin that is now possessing my body.

227
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:56,400
Now, what will it be, I wonder?

228
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:05,200
I call upon the power of the forest spirits and combine it with my own

229
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:09,540
to create a nin beast capable of consuming the nin abilities of others.

230
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:14,880
It's a big one.

231
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:18,820
As I feared, the bomber's countdown is a powerful nin.

232
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:23,900
So, how'd it go?

233
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:25,040
Did he disarm them yet?

234
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:27,440
Now book.

235
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:30,860
Okay.

236
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,680
81 specified slot card types.

237
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:36,020
They're here, all right.

238
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,240
Look, we did everything you wanted.

239
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:40,520
So now, disarm all the bombs.

240
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:43,560
But of course, I'm a man of my word.

241
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,980
But first, you need to hand over three leave cards.

242
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:51,480
Okay, then.

243
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,140
Looks like we have a deal.

244
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:54,360
Sub, borrow.

245
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:54,420
Sub, borrow.

246
00:14:57,440 --> 00:15:18,340
Here goes.

247
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,760
Release.

248
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:50,000
I just released all of you from your fear.

249
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:58,000
That...wasn't...our...deal.

250
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:07,000
You're all losers, and I don't keep promises to losers. Release doesn't disarm. It's the trigger word.

251
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Leave on!

252
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:20,000
At least now I don't have to worry about exploding.

253
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:27,000
But I'm stuck with this guy until Ginthru reverses his ability or dies.

254
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:34,000
I've got myself a troublesome companion.

255
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Hey, be still!

256
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
The bomber's going to kill us all.

257
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:48,000
He'll assume he succeeded. I'll use it to my advantage.

258
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Bisky?

259
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Hmm?

260
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
I think we should go drop by their hideout real fast.

261
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Time's probably already up for them.

262
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Besides, he didn't even tell us where it is.

263
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:16,000
And even if we could find it, we'd still need a spell card that could take us there and we simply don't have one.

264
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:21,000
I know. But some of them could have survived the explosion. It's possible.

265
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:29,000
But doubtful. If the bomber's powerful enough to place bombs on his targets without them noticing, he'd never be that careless.

266
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:37,000
However, if we just continue to play the game, then we're bound to run into the bomber at some point.

267
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:42,000
And given that fact, then sooner or later we may need to visit their hideout.

268
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:49,000
But we still need spell cards. Let's go to Masadora and sell our monster cards to buy some.

269
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Yeah!

270
00:17:50,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Hey, Bisky. How long do you think it'll take me to master my signature move?

271
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Well, you are just starting to develop your Nen. Hard to say when your power and speed will peak.

272
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,000
It is?

273
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:12,000
That said, I'd be more than a little bit surprised if it took you very long to get the form down.

274
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Really? How long?

275
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Let me see. Hmm.

276
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:21,000
